  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data view:** `Kibana Sample Data Logs` (`kibana_sample_data_logs`). Its time field is `@timestamp`. The useful fields are `response` (a string, with `response.keyword` for exact matches), `clientip`, `bytes`, `geo.dest`, `url`, and `extension`.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-e50a91b3 Web logs overview`** (`eff-e50a91b3-web-logs-overview-e2ab2e85b297`)\n- Total requests (count metric)\n- Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n- Requests over time (line chart, date histogram on `@timestamp`)\n- Requests by response code (bar chart, terms on `response.keyword`, top 10)\n\nThe time range is set to the last year, because I don't know when the sample data was loaded. Narrow it if the data is recent.\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-e50a91b3 5xx spike`** (id `6ff8678b-cb00-40b2-9e3c-44688caea943`)\n- Type `.es-query`, runs every 1m, consumer `stackAlerts`\n- Query: `response.keyword` matches `5??` (any 5xx code)\n- Window: last 5 minutes. Fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- Status: enabled. Alerting health is OK, with an encryption key configured.\n\nI did not verify the rule's results against the data. I couldn't query Elasticsearch directly: the raw API key returns 401 on the direct Kibana API calls and the ES endpoints I tried, so I relied on the MCP tools. The rule's status is still \"pending\" because it hasn't run yet. If the sample data has no 5xx responses in the window, it won't fire, and that's expected.",
